WEBVTT

00:00:11.906 --> 00:00:13.357
Apple Pay and Google Pay.

00:00:15.139 --> 00:00:16.803
This is our checkout in the United States.

00:00:17.443 --> 00:00:18.765
At the top, two buttons:

00:00:19.277 --> 00:00:21.667
Buy with Apple Pay, and Pay with Google Pay.

00:00:22.014 --> 00:00:23.380
Lower down is the other way:

00:00:23.806 --> 00:00:26.366
type a card number, an expiry date and

00:00:26.409 --> 00:00:27.109
a security code.

00:00:27.646 --> 00:00:29.097
Here is what those two buttons change.

00:00:32.707 --> 00:00:34.371
A phone wallet keeps your card on your

00:00:34.413 --> 00:00:35.113
phone as a token:

00:00:35.523 --> 00:00:36.419
a stand-in number.

00:00:37.016 --> 00:00:39.064
When you pay, you approve with your face

00:00:39.363 --> 00:00:40.063
or your fingerprint.

00:00:40.643 --> 00:00:41.837
The token goes to the processor,

00:00:42.264 --> 00:00:42.964
and on to your bank.

00:00:43.544 --> 00:00:45.165
The shop never receives your card number.

00:00:48.427 --> 00:00:49.622
It changes one more thing.

00:00:50.262 --> 00:00:52.053
With a typed card, the bank can open

00:00:52.182 --> 00:00:53.248
its own window and ask:

00:00:53.675 --> 00:00:54.742
is this really you?

00:00:55.424 --> 00:00:57.045
On a phone in Europe, more than one

00:00:57.131 --> 00:00:59.520
time in five, the shopper never comes back

00:00:59.606 --> 00:01:00.306
from that window.

00:01:00.581 --> 00:01:02.971
An Apple Pay payment asks for no bank window:

00:01:03.483 --> 00:01:05.445
the face or the fingerprint has already answered.

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:09.802
Where do we take them?

00:01:10.424 --> 00:01:12.131
Apple Pay in seven currencies,

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:13.966
across North America and Europe.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.568
Google Pay in United States dollars only.

00:01:17.127 --> 00:01:17.937
This year so far:

00:01:18.407 --> 00:01:20.199
more than a hundred and sixteen thousand

00:01:20.455 --> 00:01:22.844
wallet payments, ninety-four in a hundred

00:01:22.972 --> 00:01:23.825
of them in North America.

00:01:24.423 --> 00:01:26.983
At checkout, about nine in ten are approved.

00:01:30.454 --> 00:01:31.990
For us, three things change.

00:01:32.544 --> 00:01:34.208
We count wallets from the processor's

00:01:34.251 --> 00:01:36.043
record, because our own payment record

00:01:36.256 --> 00:01:38.304
keeps their declines and loses their approvals.

00:01:38.726 --> 00:01:40.561
A replaced card usually keeps working,

00:01:41.073 --> 00:01:43.035
because the card network keeps the token current.

00:01:43.633 --> 00:01:44.571
And one yearly job:

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:46.705
Apple checks that we own the shop's

00:01:46.748 --> 00:01:48.497
address, and that check expires.

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.415
What comes next is proposed,

00:01:53.799 --> 00:01:54.499
not built:

00:01:54.738 --> 00:01:56.487
on a phone, show the wallet first;

00:01:56.871 --> 00:01:58.407
and bring Google Pay to Europe,

00:01:58.748 --> 00:02:00.796
where Android shoppers have no wallet today.

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:04.432
Apple Pay and Google Pay:

00:02:04.688 --> 00:02:06.096
a tap instead of typing,

00:02:06.566 --> 00:02:07.846
a face instead of a window,

00:02:08.358 --> 00:02:10.379
a token instead of a card number.

